---
const before = [
  { icon: 'fi-rr-document', title: 'Printed maps', text: 'Static, hard to read on the move, and silent about what is inside each building.' },
  { icon: 'fi-rr-flag-alt', title: 'Arrows on the walls', text: 'Helpful near a building, useless when you do not know which building you need.' },
  { icon: 'fi-rr-users-alt', title: 'Asking a guard', text: 'Works, but depends on who is around, and directions are easy to forget halfway.' },
];
---
<section class="relative py-28 md:py-36">
  <div class="wrap grid gap-14 lg:grid-cols-[.9fr_1.1fr] lg:items-center">
    <div class="relative order-2 lg:order-1">
      <div class="reveal relative overflow-hidden rounded-[1.75rem] border border-white/10">
        <img src="/img/campus-teston.webp" alt="A long open corridor at Teston Hall, NDMU" width="1400" height="1050" loading="lazy" class="aspect-[4/3.4] w-full object-cover" data-parallax />
        <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-ink via-ink/20 to-transparent"></div>
        <p class="absolute bottom-5 left-5 right-5 text-sm text-paper/90">
          Many offices sit inside open hallways like this one, so you can't see them from the walkway.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="order-1 lg:order-2">
      <p class="eyebrow reveal">The problem</p>
      <h2 class="h-section mt-5 reveal">A campus you only learn by getting lost.</h2>
      <p class="lead mt-6 reveal">
        Freshmen, visitors and parents at Notre Dame of Marbel University find their way with paper maps, signs, a 3D campus
        model and directions from staff. Those help, but none of them guide you step by step or tell you about the
        buildings you pass.
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-10 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-3">
        {before.map((b) => (
          <li class="card card-glow reveal p-5">
            <i class={`${b.icon} text-xl text-mute`}></i>
            <p class="mt-4 font-display font-semibold">{b.title}</p>
            <p class="mt-1.5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-mute">{b.text}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
